WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.080
LORRAINE CINK: Marvel Studios'
Eternals introduces us

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.840
to some incredible
new superpowers,

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.430
which is why I'm
speaking with VFX

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.200
supervisor, Stephane Ceretti.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.130
Hey, Steph.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.300
 Hey, Lorraine.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.610
LORRAINE CINK: The first time we
get to see the Eternals' powers

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.680
in modern day is when
they're in London,

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.510
and they take on
the deviant, Kro.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.460
Could you talk us
through that scene?

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.780
 Well, it's a
sequence that comes

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:25.340
a little bit early in the film.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.790
You've seen a bit of the
Deviants in past times,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.940
but in this moment we
really introduce the leader

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.410
of the deviants, which is Kro.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.960
Sersi, played by Gemma
Chan, lives in London,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.630
so we had that beautiful
location of Camden.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.530
So the deviant have
come from the river.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.720
Sersi does a bit
of transmutation

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.490
on the ground to
fight that deviant.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.730
There's also Sprite
that uses illusions

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.410
to kind of confuse the deviant,
and Icarus shows up and flies.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:58.010
So it was a good way to
introduce the characters.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.820
 You had to work with
the incredible director,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.620
Chloe Zhao.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.050
Did she give you any
particular direction as you

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.459
began to work on this scene?

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:07.700
 She comes with a background
of shooting on location,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.020
shooting in nature.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:10.850
So one of the approach
for the filming

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.040
was really to try and shoot on
location as much as possible.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.350
So we tried to keep the shoot
as loose as possible to really

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:23.570
frame the actors, how they move
and how the camera is moving.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.890
Chloe really likes very
wide lenses as well,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.910
so you see a lot of the
environment all the time, which

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.740
creates some complication
for us because you

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.840
see much more than you usually
see when you use longer lenses.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.640
 Definitely.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.370
So let's talk about a
few of these moments,

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.390
like when Sprite manifests all
of these different illusions

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:45.800
of her and Sersi in order
to confuse the deviant, Kro.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.190
What was the process like
for creating that sequence?

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:52.670
 We had to do a mixture
of shooting on location,

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:57.230
then shooting multiple passes
with motion-control cameras

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:59.600
of the actresses on
a blue-screen stage,

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:02.330
and being in different
positions for every shot,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.070
creating that
library of elements

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.650
and, matching the light
that we had on the bridge.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.440
And then also, further
away from the camera,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.880
we could use digital doubles.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.610
So animated versions
of Sprite and Sersi

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.820
that we could duplicate and
animate in the background,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.520
and make it feel like
there's multiple versions

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.230
of the two characters.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.000
LORRAINE CINK:
That's incredible.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.920
All right, let's talk
about one of the moments

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.740
that is so surprising,
but also so beautiful.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:31.130
That moment when Sersi turns
the bus into rose petals.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.860
What was the process like for
bringing that moment to life?

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.870
 One complexity
of that moment was

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:37.680
to make it a believable moment.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.850
So the premise was really
mostly about trying

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.090
to find the right dynamic, the
right animation for the bus,

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:47.060
and for Icarus and
Kro hitting it.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:50.390
So that was pretty important
for us to know all the distance

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.970
and the speed of the
bus, and where everybody

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.620
had to be at that
moment to make sure

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.420
that everything was in place.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.200
Then after that, we had a
bus on the day for the shoot.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.900
The bus that you actually
see coming in the street

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:03.950
is a digital bus.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.540
We scanned the bus--

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.550
the London bus-- and
replicated it in the computer,

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.740
and it's a digital bus.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.650
The only thing that we had left
of the bus, really, at the end

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:17.060
was the actual bus driver who is
a real bus driver from London.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.760
The idea was that he was
buried under these pedals--

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.490
pretty much all the petals
you see in the sequence

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:22.290
are digital.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.350
We had a few little red
petals on the floor,

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:28.100
but clearly not enough to do
everything we needed to do.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.910
I really like the
moment of the bus,

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.700
actually, because I really like
the unexpected nature of it.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.030
We tend to do a lot of
destruction in our films,

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.250
you know, and this wasn't
a moment like that.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.230
It was a moment of
danger that transforms

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.740
into a moment of beauty.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.490
And it's kind of
magical and whimsical.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.340
It makes the movie a little
bit unique, in that sense.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.500
 The scene is so
incredible, but looking

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.340
back at the entire film,
what are you most proud of?

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.030
 There's so many
things in this film.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.690
We're creating all
these old civilisations,

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.490
and we're nowadays,
and then there's

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.170
stuff happening in space.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:06.710
We've really worked really hard
to trying to convey the idea

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.270
that the events
that were happening

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.130
were happening on
a planetary level.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:13.010
Conveying that scale in
simulation and effects

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.020
and all that stuff was
really complicated.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.610
I'm very proud of what the teams
at our visual effects studios

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.060
have done, and how much they've
put their heart into it.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.310
 Absolutely excellent work,
and thank you so much, Steph.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.110
 You're welcome.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:27.980
Thank you so much.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.230
 Everyone, go experience
Marvel Studios'

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.200
Eternals, only in theaters now.

